# Root ignore rules for demo-bank.
#
# Scope: cross-cutting IDE, editor and OS noise only. Per-project build output
# (node_modules/, .next/, .cache/, target/, build/) stays in each project's own
# .gitignore, since what counts as output differs per toolchain.
#
# Note: .gitignore only affects UNTRACKED files. Anything already committed stays
# tracked until explicitly removed with `git rm --cached`.

# --- IDE: user-local state, never portable ---------------------------------
# Absolute machine paths, window layouts, per-user build configs.
.settings/
.idea/
*.iml
*.pro.user
*.pro.user.*
CMakeLists.txt.user
CMakeLists.txt.user.*
*.suo
*.user
.vs/
nbproject/private/

# Kept deliberately: .project, .cproject, .classpath
# These let Eclipse and CDT import a project directly and are portable.

# --- Editor and tooling temp files -----------------------------------------
~AutoRecover.*
*~
*.swp
*.orig
*.rej

# --- Compiled output --------------------------------------------------------
*.class
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.elf
*.hex

# Exception: prebuilt native library the JNA sample loads at runtime, so the
# demo runs without a C toolchain. Source lives in interop/java-jna/pure-c-library/.
*.dll
!interop/java-jna/consumer/src/main/resources/JavaJnaPureCLibrary.dll

# --- MSVC / .NET build directories ------------------------------------------
# Hoisted from VisualStudio/.gitignore so projects keep these rules after being
# moved out of that directory during the reorganization.
[Dd]ebug/
[Dd]ebugPublic/
[Rr]elease/
[Rr]eleases/
[Xx]64/
[Xx]86/
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.userprefs

# --- Servlet / Tomcat runtime scratch ---------------------------------------
tomcat_tmp/
**/WEB-INF/classes/

# --- OS metadata ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
